  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1243 PM CDT Fri Jul 17 2026\n\nWV imagery indicates a broad upper level ridge of high \npressure locked in across the Western High Plains. Near the \nsurface, a weak lee side trough of low pressure remains anchored\nin eastern Colorado.\n\nRelatively dry conditions will persist early in the period \nwith the SREF indicating very little change to the \naforementioned pattern across the region. An extremely weak flow\naloft combined with marginal instability/deep layer shear will \nkeep precip chances at bay for the most part through the \nweekend. Near seasonal temperatures are forecast tonight with \nlows in the 60s(F) to the lower 70s(F). A gradual warming trend \nis likely through the weekend as high pressure dominates aloft \nwhile prevailing southerlies continue to draw warmer air into \nthe area, pushing H85 temperatures up around 25C in central \nKansas to near 30C in vicinity of the Colorado line Saturday. \nLook for widespread afternoon highs in the 90s(F) with the HREF \nindicating a 70-90% probability of temperatures exceeding 90F. \nExpect highs pushing 100F by early next week.",
